response:
 To find the value of "x" based on the given system of equations, you can first use MATLAB to solve for "a", "b", and "c" as follows:
```MATLAB
syms a b c x
% Define symbols for coefficients and constants
p = sym('p');
q = sym('q');
r = sym('r');
% Define equations
eq1 = eq(1) = ap + b*q + c*r == 28;
eq2 = eq(2) = a + b + c == 10;
eq3 = eq(3) = x == a + 2*b - c/3;
% Solve for a, b, and c
sol = solve([eq1, eq2, eq3], [a, b, c]);
% Extract the values of a, b, and c from the solution
[a_val, b_val, c_val] = sol.a;
% Calculate the value of x
x_val = subs(eq3, [a, b, c], [a_val, b_val, c_val]);
% Display the result
disp(['The value of x is ', num2str(double(x_val))]);
```
