First, we need to parse the JSON data and extract the relevant information, which is the car sizes and their corresponding height ranges. We can accomplish this using JavaScript:

```javascript
const carSizeData = {
  "carSizes": {
    // The rest of the JSON data you provided
  }
};

// Extract the carSizes object
const carSizes = carSizeData.carSizes;
```

Next, we will write a function that accepts the customer's height as an argument and returns the recommended car size based on the height range in the carSizes object. This function will calculate the index of the car size that matches the customer's height range and return the corresponding car name:

```javascript
function getRecommendedCarSize(customerHeight) {
  const heightRanges = Object.values(carSizes).map((carSize) => carSize.heightRange);

  // Find the index of the height range that includes the customer's height
  const matchingHeightRangeIndex = heightRanges.findIndex((range) => {
    const heightRangeParts = range.split(" - ");
    const minHeight = parseFloat(heightRangeParts[0].slice(0, -2)); // Remove the last inch symbol
    const maxHeight = parseFloat(heightRangeParts[1].slice(0, -2)) || Infinity; // If no max height is specified, assume the customer can fit into any larger car

    return customerHeight >= minHeight && (maxHeight === Infinity || customerHeight <= maxHeight);
  });

  // Return the name of the recommended car size
  return carSizes[Object.keys(carSizes)[matchingHeightRangeIndex]].name;
}
```

