 To create a web page that elegantly showcases an image with a captivating caption beneath it while making the image a clickable link to another webpage, follow the HTML and CSS code snippet below:

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <title>Image with Caption</title>
  <style>
    #img-container {
      text-align: center;
      position: relative;
    }

    #img-container img {
      max-width: 100%;
      height: auto;
      border-radius: 5px;
      transition: transform .3s ease;
    }

    #img-container img:hover {
      transform: scale(1.05);
    }

    #img-container p {
      margin: 0;
      font-size: 0.9em;
      line-height: 1.2;
      color: #666;
      text-align: center;
      width: 100%;
      position: absolute;
      bottom: 0;
      background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8);
      padding: 1rem;
      border-radius: 0 0 5px 5px;
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <div id="img-container">
    <a href="https://www.destination.com" target="_blank">
      <img src="image.jpg" alt="Image description" />
    </a>
    <p>Caption goes here</p>
  </div>
</body>
</html>
```

This code sets up a webpage with an image contained within a `<div>` called `#img-container`. The image is linked to another webpage using the `<a>` tag, and the caption is placed as a paragraph (`<p>`) directly below the image. The CSS styles give the image a responsive design, adding a hover effect for better user engagement, and positions and styles the caption nicely.

