 Your implementation is correct for finding unique words between two small to medium-sized texts using MATLAB. However, if the size of the texts is extremely large, reading them directly into memory might cause performance issues or even run out of memory. In such cases, consider using text analytics toolboxes like Text Analytics Toolbox or Statistics and Machine Learning Toolbox in MATLAB, which can handle large text data more efficiently. Here's an example of how to use the Text Analytics Toolbox to find unique words:

First, save your text files as UTF-8 encoded text files (.txt) in the working directory.

```MATLAB
% Import documents using a document bag
docbag = bagOfWords(importDocumentSource('*.txt'));

% Find the indices of words in Text1
idxText1 = docbag.BagOfWords.Vocabulary(docbag.Bags.Document(1).DocIndex);

