 I'd be happy to help you set up Single Sign-On (SSO) using Auth0 for multiple React applications! Here's a step-by-step guide with an emphasis on maximizing both helpfulness and verbosity:

**Step 1: Create an Auth0 Account**
First, if you don't have an Auth0 account yet, sign up at https://auth0.com. After signing up, log in and create a new "Application" in the dashboard. Select the "Single Page Web Applications" option and enter a name for your application.

**Step 2: Configure Your First Application**
After creating your application, navigate to the "Domains" tab and note down the domain value (e.g., `yourapp.auth0.com`). Next, go to the "Rules" tab and add a rule to handle the Redirect URI. Add the following rule:

```javascript
function (request, reply) {
  reply.status(302).redirect('http://localhost:3001'); // replace with your React app URL
}
```

Save the rule. This will ensure that when users authenticate or authorize, they will be redirected back to your first React app after the authentication process is complete.

**Step 3: Install Auth0 Library**
In each of your React applications, install the Auth0 library by running the following command in the terminal:

```bash
npm install --save @auth0/auth0-spa-js
```

**Step 4: Configure Your React Applications**
Create an `Auth.js` file in the `src` folder of each of your React applications. Add the following code:

```javascript
import auth from '@auth0/auth0-spa-js';

const onRedirectCallback = (appState) => {
  const { returnedTo, state } = appState;
  history.pushState(null, null, '/');
  renderApp();
};

